$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Stille Couplings (Table
9). Pd(t-Bu3P)2 catalyst (2.6 mg, 0.005 mmol) and DABCO base (84 mg, 0.75
mmol) were added under an Ar atmosphere in a 5.0 mL microwave vial
containing a magnetic stir bar and Teflon-lined septum. NaCl (15 mg, 0.25
mmol) was added as an additive under a positive flow of Ar, followed by
aryl halide (0.25 mmol), stannyl reagent (0.275 mmol), and surfactant
solution (0.5 mL of 2 wt % in degassed water), respectively. The mixture
was allowed to stir vigorously for 2-18 h. After confirming full
conversion by TLC, the reaction mixture was then diluted with 2.0 mL of
EtOAc and 0.25 mL of triethylamine. The mixture was passed through a
silica gel bed and washed with EtOAc to collect the product. All volatile
solvent was removed in vacuo to obtain the crude product that was further
purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
2-Methoxy-1-(phenylethynyl)naphthalene (Table 9, entry 2). Following the
general procedure using 1-bromo-2-methoxynaphthalene (59 mg, 0.25 mmol)
and tributyl(phenylethynyl)stannane (108 mg, 0.275 mmol), the reaction
was allowed to stir for 4 h. After column chromatography, the product was
obtained as a pale yellow solid (63 mg, 99%). -1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
8.40-8.35 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.88-7.83 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 7.83-7.79
(d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.72-7.67 (dd, J = 8.1, 1.7 Hz, 2H), 7.61-7.55 (td,
J = 8.3, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.44-7.33 (m, 4H), 7.32-7.28 (d, J = 9.0 Hz,1H),
4.08 (s, 3H).41
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions (reagent)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM "Nok": A Phytosterol-Based Amphiphile Enabling Transition-Metal-Catalyzed
Couplings in Water at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Klumphu, Piyatida; Lipshutz, Bruce H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(3), 888-900

