$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Negishi Coupling. Under
nitrogen, PdCl2(dppf) (0.015 mmol) and an iodoaryl (0.5 mmol) were
dissolved in THF (0.5 mL). Then, to this THF solution was added the aryl
zinc reagent (1 mmol). The mixture, which immediately turned black, was
stirred for 2 h at 60 °C. The reaction was quenched with saturated
aqueous ammonium chloride solution, separated, and then extracted with
ethyl acetate. The organic layer was dried over sodium sulfate, filtered,
and concentrated. Purification of products was accomplished by silica gel
chromatography. 2-isopropylbiphenyl 12 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.47-7.33 (m, 7H), 7.28-7.21 (m, 2H), 3.15-3.06 (m, 1H), 1.21 (d, J = 7.2
Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (75MHz, CDCl3) δ 146.6, 142.4, 141.3, 130.2, 129.6,
128.2, 127.9, 127.0, 125.8, 125.6, 77.5, 77.3, 77.1, 29.6, 24.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Nigishi coupling, mechanism studied,
2,2'-bis-(1-methylethyl)-(1,1'-biphenyl) also detected, golve box or
Schlenk technique used, alternative preparation decreased yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Revealing a Second Transmetalation Step in the Negishi Coupling and Its
Competition with Reductive Elimination: Improvement in the Interpretation
of the Mechanism of Biaryl Syntheses
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Qiang; Lan, Yu; Liu, Jing; Li, Gang; Wu, Yun-Dong; Lei, Aiwen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2009), 131(29), 10201-10210

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME79 STEP1
$RXN



