$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Negishi Cross-Coupling Reaction Procedure. A
typical reaction was exemplified by the cross-coupling of
p-ClC6H4C-(O)NEt2 with p-MeC6H4ZnCl catalyzed by complex 9. A solution of
complex 9 in CH2Cl2 (0.05 mL, 0.005 M solution in CH2Cl2, 0.00025 mmol)
was added into a Schlenk tube, and then CH2Cl2 was removed in vacuo. To
the Schlenk tube were charged p-ClC6H4C(O)NEt2 (0.1058 g, 0.5 mmol) and
NMP (0.7 mL). The reaction vessel was put into an oil bath, which was
preset at 70 ºC. To the stirred mixture was added by syringe a
p-MeC6H4ZnCl solution (0.7 mL, 1 M solution in THF, 0.7 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred at 70 ºC for 16 h. After the solution was
cooled to room temperature, water (10 mL) and several drops of acetic
acid were successively added. The resulting mixture was extracted with
Et2O (10 mL × 3), and the combined organic layers were dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4. The Na2SO4 was removed by filtration and washed with
Et2O. The Et2O solution was concentrated by rotary evaporation, and the
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (eluted using
a 5:1 mixture of petroleum ether and ethyl acetate) to afford a white
solid (0.1326 g, 99%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on amount of catalyst, Negishi cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene-Based Nickel Complexes: Synthesis and Catalysis in
Cross-Couplings of Aryl Chlorides with ArMX (M = Mg or Zn)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Cheng; Wang, Zhong-Xia
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2009), 28(22), 6507-6514

