$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: Pd-Catalyzed Negishi
Coupling of Aryl Halides with Secondary Alkylzinc Halides. Procedure A
was used with the following changes: A THF solution of alkyl zinc halide
(1.20 mmol, 1.50-2.50 mL) was slowly added via syringe at room
temperature instead of at 0 °C. Or following general procedure B with
methyl 2-chlorobenzoate (143 μL, 1.00 mmol) and isopropyl zinc bromide
solution (2.40 mL, 1.20 mmol, 0.500 M in THF), and toluene (1.60 mL) at
room temperature for 6 h, the crude product was purified via the Biotage
SP4 (silica-packed SNAP 10 g; 0-6% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to provide a
mixture of products as a colorless oil (172 mg, 97% yield). The ratio of
the branched to the linear cross-coupled product was determined to be
30:1 by GC and 1H NMR analysis. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 7.74 (d, J =
8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (t,
J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 3.90 (3H, s), 3.75 (septet, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.28 (d, J
= 6.9 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 168.9, 149.8, 131.9,
130.0, 129.9, 126.3, 125.6, 52.1, 29.7, 24.1 (2C) ppm. IR (neat, cm-1):
2966, 1718, 1457, 1437, 1288, 1251, 1125, 1074, 761, 716. Anal. Calcd.
for C11H14O2: C, 74.13; H, 7.92. Found: C, 73.91; H, 8.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst ligand prepared and used, Negishi coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Negishi Coupling of Secondary Alkylzinc Halides with Aryl Bromides and
Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Han, Chong; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2009), 131(22), 7532-7533

